[[ ## document ## ]]
{
  "title": "2025 Partner-Owner Data Request & Organizer Summary — Summit Physical Therapy",
  "path": "engagements/summit-physical-therapy/individual-returns/2025-partner-owner-data-request.docx",
  "document": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 1,
        "text": "Summit Physical Therapy — 2025 Partner-Owner Individual Returns"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "To: Partner-owners of Summit Physical Therapy (EIN 45-1234567)\nFrom: Lucia Mendes, Senior Tax Accountant\nRe: 2025 individual income tax return information request and organizer summary\nDate: February 12, 2026"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "This memo outlines the information each partner-owner needs to provide for preparation of their 2025 individual federal and state returns, and summarizes what we already have on hand from the Summit partnership. The partnership return (Form 1065) is in process; final K-1s are expected by March 15. We are beginning individual return intake now so we can file timely extensions and, where possible, complete returns before the April 15 deadline."
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Partner-owner roster and ownership percentages (as of 12/31/2025)"
      },
      {
        "kind": "table",
        "columns": ["Partner", "Ownership %", "K-1 status", "Prior-year filing status"],
        "rows": [
          ["Dr. Meredith Hale", "40%", "Pending — partnership return in process", "Married filing jointly"],
          ["Dr. Jonathan Reyes", "35%", "Pending — partnership return in process", "Married filing jointly"],
          ["Dr. Priya Natarajan", "25%", "Pending — partnership return in process", "Single"]
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "What we already have from the partnership"
      },
      {
        "kind": "list",
        "ordered": false,
        "items": [
          "2025 partnership general ledger and trial balance (provided January 30, 2026)",
          "Bank and investment account statements — all accounts (received February 2, 2026)",
          "Payroll records and 941s (received February 5, 2026)",
          "Loan statements and interest paid on partnership debt (received February 8, 2026)",
          "Fixed asset schedule and 2025 additions (received February 10, 2026)"
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Information needed from each partner-owner"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "Please provide the following by March 20, 2026 so we can assess extension needs and begin drafting returns. Items marked with an asterisk (*) are needed even if you believe they are not taxable."
      },
      {
        "kind": "list",
        "ordered": true,
        "items": [
          "Completed and signed 2025 tax organizer (attached separately; also available in the client portal)",
          "Copies of 2025 W-2s from any employer other than Summit Physical Therapy*",
          "All 1099 forms: 1099-INT, 1099-DIV, 1099-B, 1099-MISC, 1099-NEC, 1099-R*",
          "K-1s from any other partnerships, S-corps, estates, or trusts in which you hold an interest*",
          "Mortgage interest statement (Form 1098) and property tax records for any real estate you own*",
          "Charitable contribution records: cash and non-cash (receipts, appraisals if over $5,000)*",
          "Medical and dental expense receipts not reimbursed by insurance*",
          "State and local income tax payments made in 2025, including estimated payments*",
          "Estimated tax payments made to IRS and any state for 2025 (dates and amounts)",
          "Childcare provider name, EIN, and amounts paid (for Dependent Care Credit)",
          "Education expenses: 1098-T, student loan interest (1098-E)*",
          "Health savings account contributions and distributions (Form 5498-SA and statements)*",
          "Retirement account contributions — traditional IRA, Roth IRA, SEP, or solo 401(k) made for 2025*",
          "Any crypto or other digital asset transactions during 2025*",
          "Foreign bank accounts or assets over $10,000 at any point in 2025 (FBAR/FinCEN 114)",
          "Gambling winnings/losses, including W-2G*",
          "Casualty or theft loss documentation",
          "Prior-year federal and state tax returns (if we did not prepare them)"
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Deadlines and next steps"
      },
      {
        "kind": "list",
        "ordered": false,
        "items": [
          "March 20, 2026 — Partner-owner information due to us",
          "March 15, 2026 — Partnership Form 1065 due (we expect to file on time)",
          "April 15, 2026 — Individual returns due; if information is incomplete by March 25, we will file Form 4868 extensions",
          "Extension filers: estimated payments for 2025 must be postmarked by April 15, 2026 to avoid penalties"
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "If you have questions about whether a particular document is needed, err on the side of sending it — we would rather review and exclude than miss a deduction. Upload documents through the secure client portal or email directly to me. I will confirm receipt of each partner's complete package within two business days."
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "Thank you for getting this to us promptly. We expect Summit to generate healthy K-1 income again this year, and we want to make sure each of you is positioned properly for your 2025 tax liability.\n\nBest regards,\nLucia Mendes\nSenior Accountant, Tax\nStonebridge Advisors"
      }
    ]
  }
}
